WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.741
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:38.413 --> 00:40.666
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

4
00:46.129 --> 00:48.131
[♪ melancholy music playing]

5
01:05.315 --> 01:06.400
[horse snorts softly]

6
01:11.947 --> 01:12.948
[sighs softly]

7
01:22.583 --> 01:23.917
Let's go.

8
01:27.379 --> 01:28.797
[horse whinnies]

9
01:37.639 --> 01:39.600
[♪ music continues]

10
01:59.911 --> 02:01.204
[♪ music fades]

11
02:01.288 --> 02:02.914
[♪ dramatic music playing]

12
02:11.298 --> 02:12.591
-[♪ music swells] -[birds chirping]

13
02:12.674 --> 02:16.386
WESTERN KINGDOM

14
02:29.316 --> 02:30.359
[♪ music fades]

15
02:32.736 --> 02:34.029
[♪ moody music playing]

16
02:34.112 --> 02:36.114
[breathing heavily]

17
02:40.869 --> 02:41.912
[door opens]

18
02:41.995 --> 02:43.080
[continues breathing heavily]

19
02:44.831 --> 02:45.999
[door closes]

20
02:46.083 --> 02:47.501
[footsteps approaching]

21
03:03.100 --> 03:04.309
[sighs heavily]

22
03:07.312 --> 03:08.355
My king.

23
03:17.906 --> 03:19.908
[♪ dramatic music playing]

24
03:26.373 --> 03:27.457
You have returned.

25
03:28.750 --> 03:30.585
[breathing heavily]

26
03:40.011 --> 03:41.012
[♪ music fades]

27
03:43.849 --> 03:45.517
[♪ moody music playing]

28
03:51.731 --> 03:53.316
You look well, Your Majesty.

29
03:56.069 --> 03:57.070
Heinrey…

30
03:58.405 --> 03:59.614
Have you forgotten?

31
04:01.324 --> 04:03.952
The green emeralds embedded in the red walls

32
04:04.619 --> 04:05.871
of our hometown.

33
04:06.580 --> 04:08.039
[wind whooshing]

34
04:09.207 --> 04:10.792
We can never return there.

35
04:15.797 --> 04:17.382
Yet, I still see it clearly.

36
04:23.346 --> 04:25.390
It was the capital of the Western Kingdom.

37
04:36.318 --> 04:38.153
-[sword swooshes] -[squelches]

38
04:45.869 --> 04:47.704
[Walton III] When the crown was first laid upon my head,

39
04:47.788 --> 04:50.207
I resolved that I would ride in no carriage

40
04:50.290 --> 04:52.334
until the harbor was ours once again.

41
04:52.417 --> 04:54.836
Until it was won from the Eastern Empire.

42
04:55.796 --> 04:57.714
We will reclaim it in a single breath

43
04:58.298 --> 04:59.758
once your health is regained.

44
05:00.467 --> 05:01.468
Heinrey…

45
05:07.808 --> 05:09.059
Soon…

46
05:11.228 --> 05:12.729
you will inherit the throne.

47
05:14.606 --> 05:15.941
Our kingdom…

48
05:16.566 --> 05:20.320
It remained strong all this time, thanks to the queen's family.

49
05:21.404 --> 05:23.240
If their support were to end…

50
05:24.282 --> 05:26.201
then our nation will fall into disarray.

51
05:26.284 --> 05:28.578
You will need to continue this alliance.

52
05:29.329 --> 05:30.330
Do you hear me?

53
05:35.877 --> 05:37.003
Queen Krista…

54
05:37.963 --> 05:39.631
You may have to wed her to do so.

55
05:50.308 --> 05:53.103
I apologize for taking her from you when we were young.

56
05:53.186 --> 05:54.312
She was my fate.

57
05:56.273 --> 05:57.274
I had dreamt…

58
05:58.191 --> 06:00.235
Dreamt of reclaiming the harbor.

59
06:00.819 --> 06:02.070
And that I would see you rise.

60
06:02.737 --> 06:04.698
Rise to our kingdom's throne willingly.

61
06:07.742 --> 06:08.869
That is not the case.

62
06:09.744 --> 06:10.787
I am so sorry.

63
06:11.580 --> 06:13.790
It is only pain you have inherited.

64
06:14.541 --> 06:15.542
My king.

65
06:16.084 --> 06:17.085
Heinrey.

66
06:20.964 --> 06:22.674
My dearest Heinrey.

67
06:22.757 --> 06:24.509
[♪ soft music playing]

68
06:24.593 --> 06:26.428
I will always be your older brother.

69
06:28.638 --> 06:29.890
[Heinrey sighs]

70
06:30.724 --> 06:32.058
[sniffling softly]

71
06:34.144 --> 06:35.645
[breath trembling]

72
06:35.729 --> 06:36.938
Yes.

73
06:37.522 --> 06:38.690
Know this.

74
06:38.773 --> 06:40.108
I will watch over you.

75
06:43.737 --> 06:45.780
I will stay at your side forever.

76
06:47.240 --> 06:48.909
[Heinrey sobs softly]

77
07:16.436 --> 07:17.646
[thunder rumbling]

78
07:31.826 --> 07:34.287
[Sovieshu] As Walton III has departed this world,

79
07:34.871 --> 07:37.582
my heart aches as though I've lost an old friend.

80
07:39.626 --> 07:42.921
I wish you to know that the Eastern Empire shares in the sorrow

81
07:43.004 --> 07:45.090
of the people of the Western Kingdom.

82
07:45.173 --> 07:49.302
I will be sure to convey Your Majesty's gracious and thoughtful words of comfort

83
07:49.386 --> 07:50.428
to King Heinrey.

84
07:50.512 --> 07:52.597
The King's succession.

85
07:52.681 --> 07:54.015
I trust it is all going well?

86
07:54.099 --> 07:56.434
Prince Heinrey, the younger brother of Walton III,

87
07:56.518 --> 07:57.519
has ascended the throne

88
07:57.602 --> 08:00.563
and is overseeing the preparations for the funeral and coronation.

89
08:01.481 --> 08:03.942
King of the West, Heinrey,

90
08:04.025 --> 08:05.985
I offer my… sincere blessings.

91
08:12.117 --> 08:13.952
So Heinrey is king now.

92
08:14.035 --> 08:15.662
[Foreign Minister] This man left the royal court,

93
08:15.745 --> 08:18.164
wandered all his life and was distant from politics.

94
08:18.248 --> 08:22.085
Even if he inherits the throne, he will be manipulated by the nobles.

95
08:24.003 --> 08:26.256
What news of the Western Elder Council?

96
08:26.339 --> 08:27.549
Is their influence still strong?

97
08:27.632 --> 08:29.592
Duke Zemensia, who controls the Council of Elders,

98
08:29.676 --> 08:31.469
shared power with the late king.

99
08:32.053 --> 08:34.055
But has not revealed what kind of new relationship

100
08:34.139 --> 08:35.515
he will demand from King Heinrey.

101
08:35.598 --> 08:39.018
I fear we'll see turmoil before the new power even settles.

102
08:39.102 --> 08:40.645
[Sovieshu] He will not be easy to deal with.

103
08:40.729 --> 08:42.897
He is a crude and sly individual.

104
08:43.773 --> 08:45.650
What do you think?

105
08:46.526 --> 08:48.153
The two of you were…

106
08:49.279 --> 08:50.697
quite close in the end.

107
08:53.408 --> 08:57.120
This coronation will bring together delegates of many nations.

108
08:57.203 --> 08:58.747
For the prestige of the Eastern Empire,

109
08:58.830 --> 09:01.249
I would advise that we select ours suitably.

110
09:03.334 --> 09:06.546
Confer with the Foreign Minister and arrange a proper delegation.

111
09:09.424 --> 09:10.717
Ah…

112
09:11.718 --> 09:13.970
Rashta's pregnancy celebration…

113
09:16.097 --> 09:17.182
I suppose…

114
09:19.059 --> 09:20.351
you will not attend?

115
09:21.478 --> 09:22.562
[Sovieshu scoffs]

116
09:23.063 --> 09:25.190
I would imagine that this is a good thing.

117
09:25.899 --> 09:29.069
The noble ladies wish to gather and celebrate this child

118
09:29.152 --> 09:30.653
and they may feel uncomfortable…

119
09:32.363 --> 09:34.115
being mindful of you.

120
09:45.543 --> 09:50.507
Uh, so when do you plan to lift the banishment on Sir Kosair?

121
09:50.590 --> 09:51.883
Or is he still forbidden?

122
09:52.592 --> 09:54.469
That depends on Rashta's condition.

123
09:54.552 --> 09:56.429
If she worsens, and she may,

124
09:56.513 --> 09:57.931
he must handle the consequences.

125
09:58.014 --> 10:00.308
I do not take this decision lightly.

126
10:02.310 --> 10:04.312
[♪ soft, mysterious music playing]

127
10:26.292 --> 10:28.086
I asked Annie to spy, Your Majesty.

128
10:28.670 --> 10:31.172
She was to gain information from the Rose Room.

129
10:31.256 --> 10:34.843
Sir Artina noticed someone suspicious kept visiting Ms. Rashta,

130
10:34.926 --> 10:36.302
so I wanted to find out more.

131
10:37.387 --> 10:38.596
Visiting Rashta?

132
10:39.597 --> 10:42.433
-Who was it? -Ms. Rashta's old master.

133
10:42.517 --> 10:43.768
Lotteshu, Your Majesty.

134
10:45.145 --> 10:46.896
And that man has been here?

135
10:47.480 --> 10:49.566
-His Majesty, is he aware? -It does not seem so.

136
10:49.649 --> 10:51.359
[Eliza] That is not all, Your Majesty.

137
10:51.442 --> 10:52.777
It concerns Rashta.

138
10:53.361 --> 10:54.404
She has been…

139
10:54.487 --> 10:56.072
extorted for money by that man.

140
10:56.156 --> 10:58.616
[♪ ominous music playing]

141
10:58.700 --> 10:59.742
[coins clinking]

142
11:01.035 --> 11:02.704
This is the last time, all right?

143
11:03.621 --> 11:04.664
I have nothing else.

144
11:13.923 --> 11:15.008
[Rashta grunts in pain]

145
11:18.386 --> 11:21.014
[Navier] He must have something he is using against her.

146
11:21.097 --> 11:22.765
[Eliza] That is also my assumption.

147
11:24.350 --> 11:25.977
But what could he be holding over her?

148
11:28.313 --> 11:29.981
Hard to say.

149
11:30.064 --> 11:32.692
I heard he only recently moved to the capital.

150
11:35.653 --> 11:37.488
If you command it,

151
11:37.572 --> 11:40.033
I will investigate Viscount Lotteshu's movements.

152
11:40.116 --> 11:42.243
[♪ music continues]

153
11:47.957 --> 11:49.125
[women chuckle softly]

154
11:52.170 --> 11:53.588
[♪ music fades]

155
11:53.671 --> 11:55.215
[Albani] Good heavens!

156
11:55.840 --> 11:58.927
They say, since the New Year, this is the biggest party they've seen.

157
11:59.010 --> 12:00.386
[Albani chuckles]

158
12:03.473 --> 12:05.808
[♪ gentle music playing]

159
12:07.060 --> 12:08.102
[Rashta] My baby,

160
12:08.811 --> 12:10.563
do you hear the commotion outside?

161
12:11.648 --> 12:14.901
Those arrogant nobles have all come here to see you.

162
12:15.485 --> 12:17.862
The people who despised me as a lowly slave

163
12:17.946 --> 12:21.616
are now lining up, holding treasures of gold and silver,

164
12:21.699 --> 12:22.992
trying to win your favor.

165
12:24.369 --> 12:28.414
Those same people will all be bowing at your feet one day.

166
12:28.498 --> 12:29.958
[Albani sighs, clears throat]

167
12:32.919 --> 12:33.920
[Rashta gasps]

168
12:37.340 --> 12:38.341
[Albani] Mmm.

169
12:40.885 --> 12:42.095
Your Majesty.

170
12:45.181 --> 12:46.599
Are you not tired?

171
12:47.100 --> 12:48.685
I am quite well.

172
12:56.109 --> 12:57.527
Where's the ring?

173
12:57.610 --> 12:58.611
The ring?

174
12:59.153 --> 13:00.154
Yes.

175
13:00.238 --> 13:02.782
I'm talking about the Crimson Ring.

176
13:11.958 --> 13:13.543
[♪ ominous music playing]

177
13:16.963 --> 13:18.339
Ah…

178
13:18.423 --> 13:21.426
My fingers were swollen, so I removed it for respite.

179
13:22.010 --> 13:23.261
[sighs]

180
13:23.344 --> 13:25.930
That is a ring of healing. You should keep it on.

181
13:26.889 --> 13:28.016
That ring…

182
13:28.099 --> 13:29.142
It will keep you healthy.

183
13:30.518 --> 13:31.519
Oh?

184
13:31.602 --> 13:34.647
When I first met you, your body was covered in scars.

185
13:36.733 --> 13:38.109
The ring is enchanted.

186
13:38.609 --> 13:40.361
Wearing it quickened your healing.

187
13:41.154 --> 13:42.822
It is a mystical treasure.

188
13:42.905 --> 13:45.283
An ancient heirloom of the imperial family.

189
13:45.366 --> 13:46.451
[Rashta] Mmm.

190
13:46.534 --> 13:48.077
[footsteps approaching]

191
13:50.621 --> 13:51.789
Please, Your Majesty…

192
13:59.380 --> 14:00.465
[Rashta sighs]

193
14:00.548 --> 14:03.134
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

194
14:09.974 --> 14:11.476
[clicking]

195
14:19.358 --> 14:20.485
[banging on door]

196
14:25.907 --> 14:27.366
[Lotteshu's servant] What do you want?

197
14:38.586 --> 14:39.754
Who?

198
14:41.422 --> 14:42.548
Why?

199
14:43.132 --> 14:45.676
I have been sent to collect something urgently.

200
14:46.427 --> 14:47.470
What?

201
14:48.012 --> 14:49.806
The ring with the crimson gemstone.

202
14:51.432 --> 14:54.018
-Ah… -I was ordered to bring the ring back.

203
14:54.102 --> 14:55.436
I'm afraid it's gone.

204
14:56.020 --> 14:57.021
I'm sorry?

205
14:57.605 --> 14:58.606
May have sold it.

206
14:59.607 --> 15:00.775
[gasps] Oh no!

207
15:01.859 --> 15:03.444
You have to find it right away.

208
15:03.528 --> 15:06.364
If you cannot find that ring, then we will all be killed.

209
15:06.447 --> 15:08.866
The Emperor has been asking after it.

210
15:12.120 --> 15:13.663
Are you saying he knows about it?

211
15:13.746 --> 15:16.541
He has told Lady Rashta that she has to wear it all the time now.

212
15:16.624 --> 15:19.252
If it is revealed that you took it, then Rashta,

213
15:19.335 --> 15:21.170
you and me also…

214
15:21.629 --> 15:23.673
We will all be dead. Do you understand?

215
15:24.924 --> 15:25.925
Wait there, girl.

216
15:26.008 --> 15:27.009
I'll be right back.

217
15:28.302 --> 15:30.179
[♪ tense music playing]

218
15:31.430 --> 15:32.598
[grunts in frustration]

219
15:41.482 --> 15:42.567
[sighs]

220
16:16.225 --> 16:17.268
[cup clatters]

221
16:26.777 --> 16:27.945
[♪ music fades]

222
16:32.116 --> 16:33.117
[sighs]

223
16:35.995 --> 16:37.205
[Falhan] You have to eat something.

224
16:37.288 --> 16:38.998
At this rate, you'll starve yourself.

225
16:42.501 --> 16:43.586
[chair scraping]

226
16:44.545 --> 16:46.505
PAWNSHOP THIS MONTH'S AUCTION ITEMS LIST

227
16:47.506 --> 16:48.633
What's this?

228
16:48.716 --> 16:50.218
It's from the auction house across the street.

229
16:50.301 --> 16:52.261
This is the list of items for sale.

230
16:52.345 --> 16:55.806
It has something on there I think you'll find very interesting.

231
16:55.890 --> 16:57.433
[♪ curious music playing]

232
16:59.894 --> 17:02.688
[Kosair] Is this not the Emperor's ring?

233
17:03.522 --> 17:04.732
The crimson stone?

234
17:06.609 --> 17:08.444
Listed at the pawn shop for sale?

235
17:08.986 --> 17:09.987
[gasps softly]

236
17:21.999 --> 17:23.209
Open the door.

237
17:23.292 --> 17:25.086
Are you there? Open the door!

238
17:26.671 --> 17:27.797
Open up, hurry!

239
17:27.880 --> 17:29.966
[shop owner] There must be something in the air tonight.

240
17:30.800 --> 17:32.510
We're closed now. You'll have to--

241
17:33.052 --> 17:34.470
Oh… Viscount.

242
17:34.554 --> 17:36.806
I need the item I sold to you for the auction.

243
17:36.889 --> 17:37.890
Quickly.

244
17:37.974 --> 17:39.058
Uh… You see…

245
17:39.684 --> 17:41.269
-Um… -What?

246
17:41.936 --> 17:42.979
Where is it?

247
17:44.230 --> 17:45.606
[Kosair] Looking for this?

248
17:47.692 --> 17:49.235
[shop owner] That's the man you need to talk to.

249
17:49.318 --> 17:51.612
Ah, you already sold it. [sighs]

250
17:54.532 --> 17:55.741
[exhales deeply]

251
17:57.743 --> 18:00.204
I've decided I won't be selling the ring.

252
18:00.288 --> 18:02.582
So you really ought to return it.

253
18:03.583 --> 18:05.501
The price has gone up a fair bit.

254
18:07.461 --> 18:09.422
I do hope we can strike a deal.

255
18:09.505 --> 18:10.506
[Lotteshu] A deal?

256
18:11.215 --> 18:12.341
[chuckles scornfully]

257
18:12.425 --> 18:13.467
Ah…

258
18:14.135 --> 18:16.095
Ah, you must be an outsider.

259
18:17.513 --> 18:19.348
I am Lotteshu. It's nice to meet you.

260
18:20.016 --> 18:21.392
If you were from around here,

261
18:21.475 --> 18:23.519
you would have heard my name at least once.

262
18:24.687 --> 18:26.480
Anyway, it's not important.

263
18:26.564 --> 18:28.107
This is urgent.

264
18:28.190 --> 18:29.442
So how about--

265
18:29.525 --> 18:31.193
[both grunt]

266
18:32.695 --> 18:34.113
I am aware of you.

267
18:34.655 --> 18:35.656
And you…

268
18:36.157 --> 18:37.533
will have heard the name Kosair.

269
18:37.617 --> 18:38.951
Kosair?

270
18:39.869 --> 18:40.995
The iron-blooded?

271
18:44.123 --> 18:46.542
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

272
19:09.231 --> 19:11.067
Five thousand to kill him.

273
19:13.319 --> 19:14.403
Ten thousand…

274
19:15.029 --> 19:16.280
if captured alive.

275
19:33.047 --> 19:34.256
[grunting softly]

276
19:39.553 --> 19:40.763
[gasps]

277
19:43.307 --> 19:44.433
[chuckles scornfully]

278
19:48.437 --> 19:49.438
This ring.

279
19:49.522 --> 19:52.024
That wench gave it to you, didn't she?

280
19:52.108 --> 19:54.568
Who is "that wench," sir?

281
19:54.652 --> 19:58.197
She is now the Emperor's Mistress, but she was once your slave girl…

282
19:58.614 --> 19:59.615
Rashta.

283
20:00.908 --> 20:02.284
Will you not answer?

284
20:02.952 --> 20:04.161
Yes.

285
20:04.245 --> 20:05.246
So…

286
20:06.163 --> 20:07.707
Now you blackmail her.

287
20:07.790 --> 20:11.836
How did you do it? Threaten her? To expose her lowly history?

288
20:14.380 --> 20:16.882
Is that how you're extorting money from her?

289
20:19.385 --> 20:20.469
Yes.

290
20:20.553 --> 20:21.554
That's why.

291
20:21.637 --> 20:22.847
My lord.

292
20:23.389 --> 20:24.849
-[Kosair grunts] -[Lotteshu groans]

293
20:25.433 --> 20:27.101
[Lotteshu breathing shakily]

294
20:27.893 --> 20:29.270
It is not wise to lie.

295
20:29.353 --> 20:31.564
[Lotteshu whimpering]

296
20:32.189 --> 20:34.608
It is no secret that Rashta was once a slave.

297
20:34.692 --> 20:36.527
The Emperor is aware.

298
20:37.027 --> 20:39.029
How do you plan to use it against her?

299
20:40.364 --> 20:41.991
Unless that is not all.

300
20:42.575 --> 20:43.659
Right?

301
20:46.412 --> 20:48.080
[Lotteshu whimpering]

302
20:48.164 --> 20:51.000
There is another secret you and Rashta are withholding

303
20:51.083 --> 20:54.044
which the Emperor cannot discover under any circumstances.

304
20:55.713 --> 20:56.756
Tell me.

305
20:57.298 --> 20:58.466
[whimpers]

306
20:59.341 --> 21:01.761
-[exclaims] -And if you lie again,

307
21:02.386 --> 21:04.930
then I shall gouge out this eye to match.

308
21:06.307 --> 21:07.975
All right, all right, all right!

309
21:08.058 --> 21:10.227
There's a baby, all right? A baby!

310
21:10.311 --> 21:11.937
She is hiding a baby. Stop…

311
21:13.981 --> 21:15.107
What?

312
21:15.775 --> 21:16.776
Say that again.

313
21:18.277 --> 21:20.488
Rashta had a child before.

314
21:23.365 --> 21:24.450
[scoffs]

315
21:25.576 --> 21:26.577
No way.

316
21:26.660 --> 21:28.621
Who is the father of this baby?

317
21:28.704 --> 21:32.291
That girl… bewitched my son with her looks.

318
21:34.001 --> 21:35.586
[Kosair laughing]

319
21:37.296 --> 21:40.007
The child that Rashta had…

320
21:40.758 --> 21:41.884
is your grandchild?

321
21:41.967 --> 21:43.844
Rashta used him as leverage.

322
21:43.928 --> 21:45.846
Said my son should wed her for it.

323
21:46.514 --> 21:49.850
And then she ran away after I punished her insolence.

324
21:50.726 --> 21:51.852
[Kosair] So, she ran away…

325
21:51.936 --> 21:54.021
[♪ tense music playing]

326
22:00.152 --> 22:01.278
[Kosair sighs]

327
22:08.160 --> 22:10.079
[Kosair mutters softly] Rashta, that bitch…

328
22:19.588 --> 22:20.756
Who's there?

329
22:24.051 --> 22:25.219
It's me, sir.

330
22:25.302 --> 22:26.428
Oh.

331
22:26.512 --> 22:27.513
And who are they?

332
22:27.596 --> 22:28.931
Charles sent these men.

333
22:29.014 --> 22:30.057
Charles?

334
22:30.140 --> 22:32.059
-[door bangs open] -[gasps]

335
22:38.649 --> 22:40.985
Why, you sons of bitches! [grunts]

336
22:41.068 --> 22:42.695
[Kosair yelling]

337
22:48.701 --> 22:50.077
[exclaiming]

338
22:51.537 --> 22:54.206
Hey, Kosair! Untie me before you leave!

339
22:56.166 --> 22:57.209
[grunting]

340
23:03.007 --> 23:04.884
[Kosair] Be sure to deliver this ring to the Empress.

341
23:04.967 --> 23:06.302
And listen, it's about Rashta--

342
23:06.385 --> 23:07.428
I heard every word.

343
23:07.511 --> 23:09.430
[chuckles] Excellent.

344
23:09.513 --> 23:11.140
[Kosair yelling]

345
23:11.223 --> 23:12.766
[Artina grunting]

346
23:36.832 --> 23:39.376
You cannot get caught up in this, or Navier will be in danger.

347
23:39.460 --> 23:41.337
-Sir, what about you? -You must leave.

348
23:41.837 --> 23:43.255
That is an order!

349
23:43.339 --> 23:44.924
[♪ music swells]

350
23:46.467 --> 23:47.801
[Kosair yelling]

351
23:56.936 --> 23:58.270
[♪ music fades]

352
24:10.407 --> 24:12.660
[muffled] Huh? What's this? Where are we?

353
24:12.743 --> 24:14.244
Wait! Wait!

354
24:16.038 --> 24:17.039
Hey, wait a minute!

355
24:17.581 --> 24:18.582
Where are we going?

356
24:18.666 --> 24:20.793
Where are you taking us?

357
24:20.876 --> 24:22.419
Will someone answer me?

358
24:22.503 --> 24:24.046
Hey, wait. Wait!

359
24:24.129 --> 24:25.422
[screaming] Where are we going?

360
24:28.968 --> 24:30.177
[gate closes]

361
24:37.017 --> 24:38.102
[door opens]

362
24:39.395 --> 24:40.479
[Heinrey sighs]

363
24:42.064 --> 24:44.233
Did you not sleep at all last night?

364
24:45.901 --> 24:47.361
[McKenna continues blowing]

365
24:47.444 --> 24:49.321
What are you reading that has you so absorbed?

366
24:49.405 --> 24:51.156
The list of royal capital,

367
24:51.949 --> 24:53.701
the deployment of soldiers,

368
24:53.784 --> 24:55.703
tax collection for the Empire.

369
24:55.786 --> 24:57.287
[sighs] There's no end.

370
24:58.455 --> 25:01.583
To think my brother handled this whilst ill…

371
25:04.712 --> 25:06.588
So, what are you going to do…

372
25:08.674 --> 25:10.509
regarding Lady Krista?

373
25:16.473 --> 25:18.976
You mentioned that you plan to stand against the council.

374
25:21.145 --> 25:23.439
The nobles have somehow already begun treating

375
25:23.522 --> 25:26.233
the marriage between the two of you as a guarantee.

376
25:26.817 --> 25:28.152
What do you think?

377
25:28.235 --> 25:29.236
[McKenna] Me?

378
25:30.446 --> 25:34.992
Well, Your Majesty, I plan to stick by you whatever you decide.

379
25:36.326 --> 25:38.328
As I have always done and always will.

380
25:38.412 --> 25:41.957
Even if I stand against everyone else, and get chased out of the kingdom?

381
25:42.041 --> 25:45.085
Well then, I shall be chased off with you, Your Majesty.

382
25:45.169 --> 25:47.504
Who is the one person who will devote his loyalty to you,

383
25:47.588 --> 25:49.882
and remain by your side until the end?

384
25:50.466 --> 25:51.550
It is me, McKenna.

385
25:56.430 --> 25:57.848
Is that true for everything?

386
25:59.475 --> 26:00.601
My one condition…

387
26:00.684 --> 26:02.352
[♪ melancholy music playing]

388
26:02.436 --> 26:03.854
It cannot be Navier.

389
26:04.563 --> 26:05.981
As long as it is not her,

390
26:06.607 --> 26:08.776
I will support you no matter whom you take as your wife.

391
26:09.443 --> 26:10.736
And now you know.

392
26:11.487 --> 26:12.488
I am with you.

393
26:19.745 --> 26:20.788
McKenna.

394
26:22.414 --> 26:23.707
Yes, Sire?

395
26:24.583 --> 26:25.876
You know what?

396
26:26.919 --> 26:28.295
I miss her terribly.

397
26:32.841 --> 26:34.051
The rising sun…

398
26:35.594 --> 26:37.304
the blushing pink of sunset…

399
26:39.306 --> 26:40.599
When I open my eyes

400
26:41.183 --> 26:42.434
and when I close them.

401
26:43.977 --> 26:45.229
Every flower.

402
26:45.854 --> 26:47.314
The soft glow of the moon.

403
26:49.608 --> 26:51.485
Any beauty in this world…

404
26:53.028 --> 26:54.738
brings thoughts of Navier.

405
26:57.157 --> 26:58.992
I am powerless to it.

406
27:00.494 --> 27:01.995
Glimpses are everywhere.

407
27:03.122 --> 27:04.123
Her fragrance…

408
27:12.840 --> 27:14.800
[♪ music continues]

409
27:22.558 --> 27:24.309
[♪ music swells]

410
27:38.615 --> 27:40.158
[birds chirping]

411
27:47.916 --> 27:49.918
[♪ music fades]

412
27:51.962 --> 27:53.005
[door opens]

413
27:58.594 --> 27:59.928
Is there any news?

414
28:00.470 --> 28:02.139
Has Artina sent word?

415
28:02.222 --> 28:04.433
No. Nothing yet, Your Majesty.

416
28:15.235 --> 28:16.361
Kosair did that?

417
28:16.445 --> 28:17.571
[Albani] Yes, Your Majesty.

418
28:17.654 --> 28:19.948
He beat and tortured Viscount Lotteshu.

419
28:20.032 --> 28:22.534
And demanded that he reveal Ms. Rashta's weakness.

420
28:23.201 --> 28:24.912
[sighs] Rashta's weakness…

421
28:24.995 --> 28:26.705
He desired to find evidence

422
28:26.788 --> 28:29.833
that Rashta was indeed Viscount Lotteshu's slave.

423
28:29.917 --> 28:31.501
-[Sovieshu scoffs] -Your Majesty,

424
28:31.585 --> 28:34.713
it is clear to me that he wants to tarnish your child's name.

425
28:34.796 --> 28:38.884
To shackle the unborn babe with its mother's lowly past status.

426
28:38.967 --> 28:40.594
You cannot ignore this.

427
28:40.677 --> 28:42.888
Kosair will never stop, Your Majesty.

428
28:42.971 --> 28:45.682
I know in my heart that that man, he wants to…

429
28:46.642 --> 28:48.310
He wants to harm your child.

430
28:49.061 --> 28:50.145
[grunts angrily]

431
28:50.228 --> 28:52.397
That son of a…

432
28:52.481 --> 28:53.732
Please…

433
28:54.441 --> 28:56.568
You must defend the child, Your Majesty.

434
28:57.277 --> 29:00.155
Even though the baby borrowed the womb of a mistress,

435
29:00.238 --> 29:02.199
it is your royal flesh and blood.

436
29:02.282 --> 29:03.784
I have to wonder…

437
29:04.493 --> 29:07.996
whether this child is Your Majesty's last opportunity

438
29:08.914 --> 29:10.749
for a royal heir?

439
29:15.420 --> 29:16.797
Explain yourself.

440
29:18.799 --> 29:19.967
The Empress is…

441
29:20.842 --> 29:22.803
She is not capable of bearing children.

442
29:28.600 --> 29:29.851
[gasps]

443
29:29.935 --> 29:32.729
I… apologize. Were you not aware, Your Majesty?

444
29:32.813 --> 29:35.357
[♪ tense music playing]

445
29:35.440 --> 29:36.817
These allegations…

446
29:38.777 --> 29:40.278
Do you even have any grounds?

447
29:40.362 --> 29:42.030
[gasps] Good heavens!

448
29:44.783 --> 29:46.284
When you were children,

449
29:46.368 --> 29:48.120
there was an incident, Your Majesty.

450
29:48.787 --> 29:51.623
The previous empress was hosting a tea party.

451
29:51.707 --> 29:52.958
The two of you were playing,

452
29:53.041 --> 29:55.961
and I caught you stealing and eating cookies from the spread.

453
29:56.044 --> 29:57.337
Do you remember?

454
29:57.421 --> 29:58.755
[both giggling]

455
29:58.839 --> 30:00.048
[Albani gasps]

456
30:00.132 --> 30:02.801
-Did you two eat something? -[both laughing]

457
30:05.846 --> 30:07.264
[gasping softly]

458
30:13.061 --> 30:14.187
Cookies?

459
30:14.271 --> 30:16.481
Not a single one of your predecessor's mistresses

460
30:16.565 --> 30:17.607
could bear children.

461
30:18.316 --> 30:20.610
Did you believe that was a coincidence?

462
30:21.236 --> 30:22.446
No, Your Majesty.

463
30:22.529 --> 30:24.740
It was orchestrated by the previous empress.

464
30:24.823 --> 30:26.366
Each of these eight mistresses

465
30:26.450 --> 30:28.785
was to eat one of these cookies, Your Majesty.

466
30:30.370 --> 30:31.705
There is no antidote.

467
30:32.247 --> 30:33.874
She made every one infertile.

468
30:36.334 --> 30:38.420
-Pardon? -You hear right, Your Majesty.

469
30:38.503 --> 30:40.464
Once you've eaten them, you cannot conceive.

470
30:40.547 --> 30:43.508
And if someone is pregnant, it causes them to miscarry.

471
30:50.098 --> 30:51.266
[Sovieshu exhales deeply]

472
30:57.314 --> 31:00.859
Why did you hide this secret until now?

473
31:03.403 --> 31:05.280
Did you think if I was childless…

474
31:06.323 --> 31:09.951
then your own descendant would have a chance to take over?

475
31:10.035 --> 31:12.704
Your Majesty, that is not true! How could you think that of me?

476
31:13.622 --> 31:16.083
I could never commit such an act of disloyalty!

477
31:17.292 --> 31:18.376
It is because of…

478
31:18.960 --> 31:19.961
a promise.

479
31:20.045 --> 31:22.839
The previous empress asked that I take this to the grave.

480
31:22.923 --> 31:24.216
I had to.

481
31:24.299 --> 31:25.926
I had to keep my promise to her.

482
31:26.009 --> 31:27.010
[shushing]

483
31:32.224 --> 31:33.433
A promise?

484
31:37.145 --> 31:39.356
Is that what it was?

485
31:41.691 --> 31:42.692
[Albani groans]

486
31:42.776 --> 31:44.277
Did you find it amusing

487
31:45.153 --> 31:49.991
to watch the Empress and I struggle desperately to have a child

488
31:50.075 --> 31:52.202
all because of a promise?

489
31:52.285 --> 31:54.913
[straining] I was relieved Your Majesty was unaffected.

490
31:54.996 --> 31:57.165
I mean that sincerely. I really do.

491
31:57.249 --> 31:58.875
[gasping for air]

492
31:58.959 --> 32:01.711
[straining] How could I possibly have told you this?

493
32:02.546 --> 32:04.965
Oh, how it has plagued my heart!

494
32:07.551 --> 32:09.886
-[Sovieshu grunts] -[Albani gasping for air]

495
32:12.639 --> 32:14.599
[both panting]

496
32:22.941 --> 32:24.401
It can be said with certainty

497
32:25.527 --> 32:28.822
that Her Majesty was the only one affected by infertility.

498
32:30.407 --> 32:32.242
[exhales] Rashta's own pregnancy…

499
32:33.285 --> 32:35.328
It proves that very fact, Your Majesty!

500
32:35.412 --> 32:36.538
[breathing shakily]

501
32:37.205 --> 32:38.206
Lante!

502
32:42.377 --> 32:43.378
Your Majesty?

503
32:45.755 --> 32:47.549
Confine Kosair.

504
32:47.632 --> 32:51.094
Send the knights immediately and have him locked in Charles' farmhouse.

505
32:51.761 --> 32:53.597
We cannot have him wandering around.

506
32:54.306 --> 32:56.391
We must isolate him entirely…

507
32:57.184 --> 32:58.977
so he cannot contact anyone.

508
33:00.312 --> 33:01.730
[Sovieshu panting]

509
33:04.774 --> 33:06.526
[♪ music intensifies]

510
33:11.698 --> 33:12.782
Leave now.

511
33:24.753 --> 33:25.754
[door closes]

512
33:48.360 --> 33:50.528
[Albani] Not a single one of your predecessor's mistresses

513
33:50.612 --> 33:51.613
could bear children.

514
33:52.572 --> 33:55.367
Did you believe that was a coincidence?

515
33:55.450 --> 33:56.534
No, Your Majesty.

516
33:56.618 --> 33:58.703
It was orchestrated by the previous empress.

517
33:59.829 --> 34:01.915
There is no antidote.

518
34:01.998 --> 34:03.583
She made everyone infertile.

519
34:06.044 --> 34:07.087
[exhales deeply]

520
34:10.840 --> 34:11.883
[door closes]

521
34:11.967 --> 34:13.051
Is it done?

522
34:14.719 --> 34:17.013
-Have you completed the review? -[Count Norayu] Yes, Your Majesty.

523
34:17.097 --> 34:19.683
We thoroughly scoured records of past reigns

524
34:19.766 --> 34:21.601
and all the books on royal law.

525
34:21.685 --> 34:25.730
But no child born to a mistress can rise to the position of imperial heir.

526
34:25.814 --> 34:27.148
There is no precedent.

527
34:27.232 --> 34:31.987
Only Her Majesty the Empress' child can inherit the imperial throne.

528
34:41.496 --> 34:44.499
Have you seen the delegation list being prepared by the Duchy of Baltin?

529
34:44.582 --> 34:45.583
Not yet.

530
34:45.667 --> 34:48.336
You know, there are a good few wealthy merchants on there.

531
34:48.420 --> 34:50.213
They'll want the Western Kingdom's rare minerals

532
34:50.297 --> 34:52.340
and will haggle for the lowest price.

533
34:52.424 --> 34:54.009
To profit from the situation.

534
34:54.092 --> 34:56.511
Uh, shall we also include merchants?

535
34:58.179 --> 34:59.639
[door opens]

536
35:02.517 --> 35:04.853
[softly] Sir Artina has returned to the palace.

537
35:04.936 --> 35:06.605
He wants to see Your Majesty urgently.

538
35:13.570 --> 35:15.030
[Artina grunts in pain]

539
35:15.113 --> 35:16.364
Artina, you're bleeding!

540
35:17.324 --> 35:19.075
-Call the physician. -Your Majesty…

541
35:19.159 --> 35:20.535
I bear important news.

542
35:21.870 --> 35:23.872
Sir Kosair is in peril.

543
35:25.040 --> 35:26.041
What's happened?

544
35:26.708 --> 35:29.252
He said to give this to you.

545
35:37.385 --> 35:38.887
It is Rashta.

546
35:38.970 --> 35:40.221
She is already a mother.

547
35:42.265 --> 35:44.267
[gasps] There's another child?

548
35:44.809 --> 35:46.603
Lotteshu's son is the father.

549
35:46.686 --> 35:48.647
-They had a child together. -[♪ ominous music playing]

550
35:48.730 --> 35:51.191
It is a newborn, about five to six months old.

551
36:02.702 --> 36:05.205
[Eliza] Why do you hesitate, Your Majesty?

552
36:05.288 --> 36:09.334
The Albani House and Miss Rashta colluded together to deceive His Majesty.

553
36:09.417 --> 36:11.503
You have to tell him the whole truth.

554
36:13.129 --> 36:14.798
It will save Sir Kosair.

555
36:19.302 --> 36:21.262
If his knights arrived on his orders,

556
36:22.222 --> 36:23.682
His Majesty must know.

557
36:24.349 --> 36:26.476
Surely, he knows everything already.

558
36:30.939 --> 36:32.315
I am left with no choice.

559
36:33.024 --> 36:34.776
I will speak to His Majesty

560
36:34.859 --> 36:36.236
and I will save my brother.

561
36:48.164 --> 36:50.125
[♪ tense music playing]

562
36:51.876 --> 36:53.211
[door opens]

563
36:54.421 --> 36:55.505
[door closes]

564
37:01.720 --> 37:05.557
I have carried out everything as Your Majesty instructed, but I…

565
37:06.766 --> 37:08.143
[Sovieshu sighs]

566
37:08.226 --> 37:09.436
[Sovieshu] Lante.

567
37:10.854 --> 37:12.021
[Marquess Lante] Yes, Your Majesty?

568
37:18.611 --> 37:20.572
[♪ melancholy music playing]

569
37:20.655 --> 37:22.031
The Empress…

570
37:30.206 --> 37:31.666
I have to divorce her.

571
37:39.716 --> 37:41.718
[♪ dramatic music playing]

572
37:51.561 --> 37:52.729
[Annie] Your Majesty.

573
38:15.668 --> 38:17.086
[♪ music fades]

574
38:51.162 --> 38:52.455
[Rashta] What are you saying?

575
38:56.000 --> 38:57.377
What do you mean, a divorce?

576
38:58.545 --> 38:59.796
[Sovieshu] Exactly that.

577
39:00.797 --> 39:02.507
I mean to divorce the Empress.

578
39:03.925 --> 39:05.093
[Rashta] Why?

579
39:06.010 --> 39:07.095
So…

580
39:07.595 --> 39:09.347
So what is going to happen next?

581
39:22.944 --> 39:24.571
You will become the empress.

582
39:30.243 --> 39:31.411
Ah…

583
39:31.953 --> 39:33.997
The Empress will not choose to step aside.

584
39:34.873 --> 39:37.125
I know she will not take a divorce lightly.

585
39:38.084 --> 39:40.086
Her family could create issues, too.

586
39:40.169 --> 39:42.630
Hmm. I do not think so.

587
39:42.714 --> 39:44.340
So, what will you do?

588
39:46.259 --> 39:47.427
I'll take care of it.

589
39:49.178 --> 39:50.179
So do not worry.

590
39:53.892 --> 39:55.435
I will do what I can.

591
39:58.605 --> 40:02.317
[Sovieshu] You need only devote yourself to keeping your body healthy.

592
40:04.360 --> 40:07.697
And until I say, keep what we discussed today between us.

593
40:07.780 --> 40:09.490
[♪ sad, heartfelt music playing]

594
40:15.413 --> 40:16.748
[door closes]

595
40:40.146 --> 40:41.856
[breathes heavily]

596
40:45.109 --> 40:47.111
[♪ music intensifies]

597
41:17.016 --> 41:18.059
Is it really true?

598
41:22.814 --> 41:24.440
I'm to become the empress?

599
41:28.861 --> 41:30.863
[snorts, laughing]

600
41:36.911 --> 41:37.996
Rashta!

601
41:40.498 --> 41:41.624
The Empress.

602
41:45.378 --> 41:46.379
[exhales]

603
41:47.338 --> 41:49.257
Rashta, the new Empress.

604
41:50.633 --> 41:51.634
Rashta…

605
41:52.552 --> 41:53.553
Ishka…

606
41:55.054 --> 41:56.180
Botulin.

607
41:56.264 --> 41:58.099
[♪ grand music playing]

608
42:03.855 --> 42:05.606
[♪ music continues]

609
42:12.780 --> 42:14.032
[birds chirping]

610
42:22.957 --> 42:25.209
[Heinrey] What usually happens to a widowed queen?

611
42:25.293 --> 42:28.337
She would vacate the palace and move to an estate in Compshire.

612
42:28.421 --> 42:29.756
There is no formal decree,

613
42:29.839 --> 42:31.841
but that is what I learned from our records.

614
42:31.924 --> 42:33.384
Find those records.

615
42:33.468 --> 42:34.677
Yes, Your Majesty.

616
42:34.761 --> 42:35.762
[birds chirping]

617
42:40.808 --> 42:41.809
[Krista] Heinrey.

618
42:45.229 --> 42:46.898
Shall we walk together?

619
42:47.690 --> 42:49.025
Just like we used to…

620
42:49.734 --> 42:51.360
when we were children.

621
42:53.071 --> 42:54.697
[♪ soft music playing]

622
42:54.781 --> 42:56.199
When we were children?

623
42:56.783 --> 42:57.992
[Krista] Mmm.

624
42:59.827 --> 43:02.246
Are you accustomed to life at the palace yet?

625
43:02.789 --> 43:05.249
I wonder if it's because I was born here,

626
43:05.333 --> 43:07.001
the palace has embraced me quickly.

627
43:07.085 --> 43:10.338
The people, however, do not acknowledge me at all.

628
43:11.839 --> 43:14.634
The Council of Elders may be rather territorial.

629
43:14.717 --> 43:16.344
If you yield on the tax issue,

630
43:16.427 --> 43:18.513
many others will be resolved easily.

631
43:18.596 --> 43:21.766
You should be selective of your battles with them.

632
43:21.849 --> 43:25.103
You must be careful and do not fall into the trap Father left you.

633
43:25.186 --> 43:26.562
You should have patience…

634
43:27.563 --> 43:28.898
and forge a path of your own.

635
43:30.066 --> 43:32.652
You asked to go for a walk like we used to,

636
43:32.735 --> 43:34.403
but I suspect there's another reason.

637
43:35.279 --> 43:36.364
That may be the case.

638
43:36.447 --> 43:38.950
Besides, some Elders value the new king's drive.

639
43:39.033 --> 43:40.785
[Heinrey chuckles]

640
43:40.868 --> 43:42.537
You have changed.

641
43:43.412 --> 43:46.666
The power struggle between Father and the late king was rife.

642
43:46.749 --> 43:48.000
I heard as such.

643
43:48.084 --> 43:50.628
My brother had you. Your solidarity was useful to him.

644
43:52.421 --> 43:54.006
You can also use me.

645
43:54.632 --> 43:56.759
I can give strength to your voice.

646
43:58.219 --> 44:00.179
That option is there for you.

647
44:01.389 --> 44:02.431
Krista…

648
44:09.730 --> 44:11.858
Everyone has an opinion on our marriage,

649
44:11.941 --> 44:13.151
but not us.

650
44:13.234 --> 44:15.444
As we have not yet had the chance to talk.

651
44:17.155 --> 44:19.115
Royal marriages often work that way.

652
44:20.199 --> 44:22.368
A political contract is all this is.

653
44:22.451 --> 44:23.786
Our wishes are secondary.

654
44:25.580 --> 44:27.999
Our unity is a safe choice

655
44:28.082 --> 44:29.458
and a political one.

656
44:29.542 --> 44:31.377
But do you not wish for love?

657
44:31.460 --> 44:34.422
I also wish to serve the people, not just the Council of Elders.

658
44:34.505 --> 44:36.674
We are in a position to change how things are.

659
44:36.757 --> 44:38.551
The kingdom deserves a new start.

660
44:39.427 --> 44:41.220
One that I know will make us proud.

661
44:41.304 --> 44:43.639
Your thoughts on royal marriage are sound.

662
44:43.723 --> 44:45.308
Is there a lady you think of?

663
44:46.475 --> 44:47.476
Is there?

664
44:47.560 --> 44:49.020
[♪ gentle music playing]

665
44:53.316 --> 44:54.650
Yes, there is someone.

666
44:55.776 --> 44:56.986
She's the one.

667
45:12.835 --> 45:15.421
[Eliza] I heard there was a frost overnight,

668
45:16.672 --> 45:19.383
but now the weather has grown warm again.

669
45:23.888 --> 45:25.473
Have you discussed the issue…

670
45:26.057 --> 45:28.142
with Rashta? Or with His Majesty?

671
45:29.143 --> 45:30.728
What did he say?

672
45:30.811 --> 45:32.605
I did not speak to him.

673
45:35.691 --> 45:36.692
Countess Eliza…

674
45:38.194 --> 45:39.403
You said Rashta…

675
45:40.071 --> 45:42.198
will be taught by the finest of teachers?

676
45:42.281 --> 45:43.491
Yes.

677
45:43.574 --> 45:47.536
I heard His Majesty had personally selected all the tutors,

678
45:47.620 --> 45:48.871
some of whom were yours.

679
45:50.373 --> 45:54.252
Rashta will be learning everything that all the nobles do.

680
45:54.335 --> 45:57.588
Her tutorage will start at the basics, like any highborn child.

681
45:57.672 --> 45:59.715
She must memorize all of the state officials,

682
46:00.424 --> 46:01.425
the nobles…

683
46:01.968 --> 46:04.178
and the Imperial history and family tree.

684
46:04.262 --> 46:06.806
And when was this education initiated?

685
46:08.015 --> 46:09.433
After she fell pregnant.

686
46:10.476 --> 46:11.936
After she fell pregnant?

687
46:18.025 --> 46:19.527
Your Majesty,

688
46:19.610 --> 46:21.279
this evening with His Majesty is scheduled.

689
46:21.362 --> 46:24.240
You are set to have dinner with His Majesty, as usual.

690
46:24.824 --> 46:26.117
What outfit should I prepare?

691
46:28.744 --> 46:30.037
I would like a colorful one.

692
46:30.830 --> 46:32.331
-We will prepare it. -We will prepare it.

693
46:40.589 --> 46:42.591
[♪ tense music playing]

694
46:51.017 --> 46:53.686
My brother is confined under Your Majesty's orders.

695
46:54.562 --> 46:55.813
When will he be freed?

696
47:06.657 --> 47:08.701
How did you come across that knowledge?

697
47:08.784 --> 47:11.787
How could you forget that the walls have ears in this palace?

698
47:12.788 --> 47:14.623
I am aware of everything.

699
47:15.207 --> 47:16.751
I am the Empress.

700
47:20.546 --> 47:22.882
If you heard that your brother is in confinement…

701
47:24.216 --> 47:27.094
Then I assume… you know why.

702
47:27.720 --> 47:31.640
He sought gossip about Rashta, and in doing so reduced an innocent man…

703
47:32.350 --> 47:33.934
to a bloody mess.

704
47:35.728 --> 47:37.480
You call him an innocent man.

705
47:38.522 --> 47:40.232
Now, tell me, sire.

706
47:40.316 --> 47:43.194
Is this innocent man the one whose eye you removed?

707
47:43.903 --> 47:45.738
Did you not make him swear to you

708
47:46.655 --> 47:48.616
that he would never speak of Rashta again?

709
47:53.079 --> 47:54.413
I warned you of this.

710
47:54.497 --> 47:55.581
[sniffs]

711
47:56.499 --> 47:59.627
I will protect my unborn child at all costs.

712
47:59.710 --> 48:01.962
And that includes when Rashta is threatened.

713
48:13.891 --> 48:15.476
The decision is made.

714
48:16.769 --> 48:18.771
General Kosair is banished.

715
48:18.854 --> 48:20.147
You don't mean that.

716
48:20.856 --> 48:22.483
Clearly, I can no longer trust him.

717
48:22.566 --> 48:26.070
And I think that even you cannot control him now.

718
48:27.613 --> 48:30.241
And I am not convinced that that will change.

719
48:32.660 --> 48:34.745
My brother's efforts were not in vain.

720
48:36.372 --> 48:38.249
Are you even aware of what he obtained?

721
48:39.041 --> 48:42.670
Yes! He was searching for Rashta's slave documentation.

722
48:43.754 --> 48:45.172
Such things do not exist.

723
48:46.132 --> 48:48.217
Must you have such hatred for her?

724
48:48.300 --> 48:49.760
That poor, defenseless creature.

725
48:49.844 --> 48:51.470
She has lived such a pitiful life.

726
48:51.554 --> 48:54.723
She finally stands tall with humility and grace.

727
48:54.807 --> 48:58.519
Yet you are desperate to take it from her, despite having so much.

728
48:58.602 --> 49:01.981
That child has no greed, no desire, no background, and no power.

729
49:02.064 --> 49:03.691
She cannot compete.

730
49:03.774 --> 49:05.901
And yet, you are still threatened.

731
49:05.985 --> 49:07.862
That girl carries my child,

732
49:07.945 --> 49:11.365
and you and your brother, members of such an influential family,

733
49:12.908 --> 49:15.536
want nothing more than to besmirch her.

734
49:20.958 --> 49:23.419
[laughs scornfully]

735
49:30.926 --> 49:32.303
[chuckles softly]

736
49:39.560 --> 49:40.978
[chuckles]

737
49:45.399 --> 49:46.692
I have no appetite.

738
49:48.068 --> 49:49.528
It's time for me to depart.

739
50:00.331 --> 50:02.291
[♪ grand music playing]

740
50:05.252 --> 50:06.587
The coronation…

741
50:07.963 --> 50:09.798
I have decided upon the delegate.

742
50:13.219 --> 50:14.637
I will go.

743
50:14.720 --> 50:16.347
[♪ music swells]

744
50:19.350 --> 50:22.520
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

745
50:23.479 --> 50:25.481
[♪ closing theme music playing]
